title: Setup starts the server before the reader has a config, and the config it defaults to is Jeff's, which the repository does not hold.
pid: e0d95c9b-2f22-47de-8d75-ecf64b16b897
body: |2-
  "start the Skg server" comes before "set up your data folder", and
  without an argument the script uses 'data/jeff/skgconfig.toml';
  'data/jeff/' is Jeff's own data and is not in the repository, and the
  client's snippet loads the same config. "set up your data folder"
  then says "See example-data/ for how" and goes on to migrating from
  'owned_folder' and two users sharing one data tree, before the
  reader has any data. It also uses 'skgrepo' throughout, a word
  defined only in 'data-model_friendly.org', which 'docs/README.org'
  lists after setup, and which never says what a skgrepo is on disk.
  Change: make the data folder the step before the server, in two
  sentences: a skgrepo is a folder of '.skg' files, one per note,
  best kept as a git repository; copy 'example-data/' to
  'data/YOURNAME/' and give that config to the server and the client.
  Move migrating and sharing a data tree to a later page.
